# Fblthp, "You may look at the top card of your library any time. The top card of your library has plot. The plot cost is equal
# to its mana cost. You may plot nonland cards from the top of your library" (CR 702.170a, 116.2k, 401.2): on turn one Bot1
# casts Fblthp off a Black Lotus, looks at the top card, and plots the Lightning Bolt on top for exactly its mana cost {R} (a
# Mox Sapphire's {U} alone cannot pay it: the refusal, until a Mountain is played). The Bolt is exiled, so the Ornithopter under it is the new top card, and the
# Bolt cannot be cast the turn it was plotted. Bot2 has no such rule: it looks at nothing. On turn three the Bolt is cast free
# and Bot2 is at 17.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Mountain
Fblthp, Lost on the Range
Island
Island
Island
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x7
Lightning Bolt
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Fblthp, Lost on the Range.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.MayLookAtLibraryTop = true
? Bot2.MayLookAtLibraryTop = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
! Bot1.Library.Lightning Bolt.Activate(Ability: Plot; Mana: short)
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Library.Lightning Bolt.Activate(Ability: Plot)
? Bot1.Mana = {U}
? Exile = Lightning Bolt
! Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Graveyard = Lightning Bolt; Black Lotus
Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Hand = Island; Island; Island; Ornithopter
